{"request": "Write a script that creates a form which accepts and saves user-inputted text", "response": "Here is a complete, self-contained solution using **HTML**, **CSS**, and **JavaScript**.

This script creates a form that accepts text input and saves it to the browser's **Local Storage**. This means the data will persist even if you refresh the page or close the browser, without needing a backend server.

### The Solution

Save the following code as an `.html` file (e.g., `form.html`) and open it in any web browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Text Input & Save Form</title>
    <style>
        /* Basic Styling for the Form */
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f4f4f9;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
        }

        .container {
            background: white;
            padding: 2rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
            width: 300px;
        }

        h2 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #333;
        }

        label {
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        input[type="text"] {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 4px;
            box-sizing: border-box; /* Ensures padding doesn't affect width */
        }

        button {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            background-color: #28a745;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
        }

        button:hover {
            background-color: #218838;
        }

        /* Styling for the saved list */
        #saved-items {
            margin-top: 20px;
            border-top: 1px solid #eee;
            padding-top: 10px;
        }

        .saved-item {
            background: #e9ecef;
            padding: 8px;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
        }

        .delete-btn {
            background-color: #dc3545;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 4px 8px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 12px;
            margin-left: 10px;
        }

        .delete-btn:hover {
            background-color: #c82333;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="container">
        <h2>Save Your Text</h2>

        <form id="textForm">
            <label for="textInput">Enter some text:</label>
            <input type="text" id="textInput" placeholder="Type here..." required>
            <button type="submit">Save Text</button>
        </form>

        <div id="saved-items">
            <h3>Saved Items:</h3>
            <div id="list-container">
                <!-- Saved items will appear here -->
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        // 1. Select DOM elements
        const form = document.getElementById('textForm');
        const inputField = document.getElementById('textInput');
        const listContainer = document.getElementById('list-container');

        // 2. Load saved data when the page opens
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', loadSavedItems);

        // 3. Handle Form Submission
        form.addEventListener('submit', function(event) {
            event.preventDefault(); // Prevent page reload

            const text = inputField.value;

            if (text.trim() === "") {
                alert("Please enter some text.");
                return;
            }

            saveItem(text);
            inputField.value = ''; // Clear input field
        });

        // 4. Function to save item to Local Storage
        function saveItem(text) {
            // Get existing array or create new one
            let items = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('savedTextItems')) || [];

            // Add new item with a timestamp
            const newItem = {
                text: text,
                date: new Date().toLocaleTimeString()
            };

            items.push(newItem);

            // Save back to Local Storage
            localStorage.setItem('savedTextItems', JSON.stringify(items));

            // Update the UI immediately
            renderList();
        }

        // 5. Function to load items from Local Storage
        function loadSavedItems() {
            let items = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('savedTextItems')) || [];
            renderList();
        }

        // 6. Function to render the list on the screen
        function renderList() {
            listContainer.innerHTML = ''; // Clear current list

            const items = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('savedTextItems')) || [];

            if (items.length === 0) {
                listContainer.innerHTML = '<p style="color:#777; font-style:italic;">No items saved yet.</p>';
                return;
            }

            // Loop through items and create HTML elements
            items.forEach((item, index) => {
                const div = document.createElement('div');
                div.className = 'saved-item';

                div.innerHTML = `
                    <span>${item.text} <small>(${item.date})</small></span>
                    <button class="delete-btn" onclick="deleteItem(${index})">Delete</button>
                `;

                listContainer.appendChild(div);
            });
        }

        // 7. Function to delete an item
        window.deleteItem = function(index) {
            let items = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('savedTextItems')) || [];

            // Remove item at specific index
            items.splice(index, 1);

            // Save updated array
            localStorage.setItem('savedTextItems', JSON.stringify(items));

            // Re-render list
            renderList();
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

